    description: "From the WI-kosup reader census (2026-10-28; /home/jgstern_agent/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/kosup_reader_census_10282026/B_meta.md §1.2, §3a, §4). Meta-key write-only family and named decisions:\n- DECISION (replaces the 2026-10-21 'keep until their first reader', an unfireable trigger): Edge.meta call_type and method -- DELETE both. Every writer's value is already on the same edge or its source symbol (otp -> mechanism; cobol -> evidence_type; subprocess -> the source symbol's call_type; openapi -> the source symbol's http_method; ipc -> the source symbol's bridge_method).\n- DELETE export_scope (registered, never written).\n- cobol.py ~:439 replaces the whole meta dict make_unresolved_edge just wrote, so unresolved COBOL CALL edges lose callee_name (shape (ii); check-meta-write-discipline only scans subscript writes, so it cannot see this).\n- 115 of 203 registered keys have no production reader (22 not even read by a test). Verdict for the family: DECLARE EXTERNAL, with a READ-SIDE GATE that pins the write-only set exactly, so a new reader (or a lost one) changes the pinned set and fails a test -- the fireable replacement for 're-audit when a consumer appears'. The registry docstring admits reads are never checked.\n- 157 emitted keys are unregistered (130 with no reader, none in docs/schema.json): register or stop writing.\nInput for WI-kuhoh: 33 keys written on BOTH Symbol.meta and Edge.meta, each registered on one axis only (list in §3c)."  # 8f67
